          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The concept of
            %em spectral affine line
            is the generalization of the concept of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+line"} affine line
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+geometry"} spectral geometry
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+geometry"} E-∞ geometry
          %p
            Given a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connective+spectrum"}> connective
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is the affine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+scheme"} spectral scheme
            given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+symmetric+algebra"} spectral symmetric algebra
            on a single generator:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi R
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Sym
                    %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{A}^1_R = Spec( Sym_R(R) )
                  \\,.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#LurieSchemes"} Lurie Schemes, below prop. 2.20
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo =
                  %mi 𝕊
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = \mathbb{S}
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %em absolute spectral affine line
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#StricklandTurner97"} Strickland-Turner 97
          %h2#references References
          %p Some general comments are in
          %ul
            %li#LurieSchemes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              , below prop. 2.20
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spectral+Schemes"} Spectral Schemes
          %p
            The absolute spectral affine line over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo =
                  %mi 𝕊
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = \mathbb{S}
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#StricklandTurner97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Strickland"}> Neil Strickland
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Turner"} Paul Turner
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Rational Morava
                  = succeed "-theory" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D S^0
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu/Strickland-PTurner/rme.pdf"} pdf
